        bullets: ['I AM adalah definisi diri dari sang absolut', 'Fondasi di mana segala sesuatu berdasar', 'I AMness Anda adalah Tuhan — bukan secara kiasan, melainkan secara nyata'],
        fullContent: 'The most powerful words you can ever speak are "I AM." These two words are not merely a grammatical construction — they are the self-definition of the absolute, the foundation upon which all of reality rests. When Neville says "I AM is the first cause-substance," he means that your awareness of being is the creative force behind everything in your experience. Every state you enter, every condition you encounter, begins with an "I AM" — whether conscious or unconscious.\n\nMost people walk through life saying "I am broke," "I am sick," "I am unlucky," without realizing they are decreeing their reality with every utterance. The I AM does not discriminate — it accepts whatever follows it and sets about externalizing that condition. When you say "I AM" followed by any state, you invoke the creative power of the universe itself. The I AM is God\'s name eternally, and your use of it carries the same creative authority.\n\nThe practical implication is staggering: you can shift your entire experience by shifting what follows your I AM. Not through mere affirmation, but through genuinely assuming the feeling of the state you desire to occupy. The I AM is the door; feeling is the key that turns it.',
