        fullContent: 'Perhaps the most liberating and most resisted teaching Neville offers is this: you are already that which you want to be. The thing you seek does not need to be created — it already exists. You do not need to become worthy of it, earn it, or attract it. You need only to stop refusing to believe you already are it.\n\nThis is the meaning behind Neville\'s reinterpretation of Scripture. When Jesus says "Before Abraham was, I AM," he is declaring that the desired state exists eternally in the present. There is no past or future in consciousness — only NOW. The state of wealth, health, love, or any other desire exists now in the fourth dimension. Your refusal to claim it — your insistence that it is "not yet" — is the only barrier.\n\nThe resistance most people feel comes from relying on their senses. Their eyes tell them they are poor, their body tells them they are sick, their bank account tells them they lack. But these are effects, not causes. They are the out-picturing of a past state of consciousness. The present 3D world is always showing you what you HAVE assumed, not what you WILL assume. When you shift your assumption, the world must eventually conform — but there is a time lag that tests your faith.\n\nTo overcome this, you must define your desire clearly, then assume the feeling of already being it. Not "I will be" but "I am." Not "It\'s coming" but "It is done." This shift from future to present tense is the entire secret.',
